<!--Post: 11982--><!--Time: 1111480839-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11982"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 12:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is an unsolved murder in Beloit, KS. Beloit is located 10 miles East of Glen Elder, the location of Jeff Rader. There has been alot of local publicity about her murder and it being still unsolved. Carol Fleming was found shot in her home last August. I&#39;m in no way saying that she is a victim of BTK, but when the link to Jeff Rader&#39;s Hunting Lodge was posted I remembered this unsolved murder. By the way, this is VERY close to home for me....yikes! <BR>I&#39;ll keep digging ~~ see what I can find. <BR>  <BR><a href="http://www.saljournal.com/content/2-0-/module/displaystory/story_id/1176/format/html/displaystory.html" target=_top>http://www.saljournal.com/content/2-0-/module/disp laystory/story_id/1176/format/html/displaystory.ht ml</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Beloit murder frustrating <BR>Tuesday, February 17, 2004 08:49 pm <BR> <BR>People keeping quiet about homicide <BR> <BR>  <BR>  <BR> <BR>  By TIM UNRUH <BR> Salina Journal  <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR>   <BR>BELOIT — Finding Carol Fleming’s killer requires cooperation, Mitchell County Attorney Rod Ludwig said Tuesday, and to date that’s been lacking.  <BR> <BR>More than 50 people have been interviewed, including some in other states, since Fleming, 51, was gunned down in her home during the early hours of Aug. 16.  <BR> <BR>Since that night the three lead investigators on the case have each logged roughly 600 hours, Ludwig wrote in a press release. Those include lead investigator Bill Pettijohn, senior special agent with the Kansas Bureau of Investigation, Mitchell County Sheriff Doug Daugherty and sheriff’s office Investigator Wayne Loy.  <BR> <BR>The probe has led them to 30 to 40 people with knowledge of events leading up to the murder, he wrote, and “only a handful have been willing to speak to investigators.”  <BR> <BR>Ludwig said Tuesday he remained “determined,” to nab Fleming’s killer, but the suspect list is getting larger instead of smaller.  <BR> <BR> <BR>For more on this story and what law officers are doing in the investigation, read reporter Tim Unruh&#39;s story in Wednesday&#39;s Salina Journal. <BR> <BR>©2004 Salina Journal  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11982-->
<!--Post: 11983--><!--Time: 1111481082-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11983"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 12:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found more info on Carol Fleming. She was murdered in August 16, 2003. This is a more detailed press release concerning her murder. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.saljournal.com/content/2-0-/module/displaystory/story_id/1155/format/html/displaystory.html" target=_top>http://www.saljournal.com/content/2-0-/module/disp laystory/story_id/1155/format/html/displaystory.ht ml</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11983-->
<!--Post: 11993--><!--Time: 1111492815-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11993"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 4:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That was a Saturday night, who knows where he was that weekend? But I&#39;m getting some strange vibes about Fleming plus Adam. Yes, ten years apart. but if not Denny, maybe there is another one out there. Looking at location, I find it strange that a transitory would just come through there and just pick her off the top of his head. It has happened, but it&#39;s in the minority. Anyone know what her &#34;business&#34; was? Personally, I believe &#34;Christ on the Cross&#34;. I believe that he did stop, well before that was written. But maybe not before Kathyrn Adam. From what I read, I don&#39;t believe Adam involved the use of a firearm. But I believe victimology comes ahead of weapon choice to this kind of perp. Just kinda dreaming out loud here, much more specific info is needed before any real hypothesis is possible. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11993-->
<!--Post: 11995--><!--Time: 1111496844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11995"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Zenith<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Zenith<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 5:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is so little information regarding what happened in this murder that it&#39;s hard to relate it to BTK at all.  <BR> <BR>I immediately suspected the son knows more. The son&#39;s interview is completely odd. Can&#39;t see why he needed to state his alibi in detail to the media. Over-explaining....I was at a bar, came home, talked with the neighbors &#40;at 2 in the morning no less&#41;, left again, came back, was feeding the dogs... couldn&#39;t have been me man....hmmmm. <BR> <BR>However, in fairness need to state that all people don&#39;t behave as we expect when under such duress.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11995-->
<!--Post: 11999--><!--Time: 1111499239-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11999"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 5:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has anyone confirmed that the Jeff r. that runs the lodge is the same jeff that is dennys bro? <BR>I havent found it anywhere. the adress we have for the bro is Falun ks. the lodge is in glen elder. <BR>A local could call the lodge and ask, if they arent related they will say, &#34;Gosh no, thats not us&#34;, if they are related they may say &#34;no comment&#34;. Just athought, if anyone local wants to call. Or if anyone here even knows a friend living in glen elder, the gossip would be around town. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11999-->
<!--Post: 12113--><!--Time: 1111597259-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12113"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 9:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok gang ~ I called the number on the website this morning. I got voice mail. It&#39;s hard to understand the man&#39;s voice, he talks very fast. I called back three times and listened and I could only make out : &#34;You have reached Rings &amp; Sons of South Dakota, home of the finest fishing &amp; hunting in the midwest......&#34; The part I had trouble deciphering was the last name, it sounds like RINGS. Anyone else care to give it a try? The number is 785.545.3476. The South Dakota thing sort of makes me suspicious. I know a few people from South Dakota and they have a pronounced accent. The man on the recording does not have that accent.  <BR>However!! Being a rancher myself, I do know that city-slickers with money are buying up property to hunt and fish, sometimes building lodges and so forth and only using them during hunting/fishing seasons. Glen Elder does have a sizeable lake stocked with bass, stripers, catfish, etc. Also with government land surrounding the lake, the area is be full of wild game.  <BR> <BR>The summary is: <BR>1. They changed the voice mail because of Dennis Rader. <BR>2. They live in South Dakota and are not related. <BR>3. They live in South Dakota, and are related to Dennis Rader. <BR> <BR>Whaddya think?? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12113-->
<!--Post: 12114--><!--Time: 1111599270-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12114"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 9:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s called &#34;Wings and Fins of South Dakota&#34; and it is linked from the Rader Lodge website. This is only a part time operation so it&#39;s possible Jeff could be involved from Falun. Please note that the murder occurred before the start of season. Don&#39;t know that it means much though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12114-->
<!--Post: 12115--><!--Time: 1111600040-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12115"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 9:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Nightdriver!  <BR>Guess my hearing is not what it should be =&#40; <BR>What shall I do next? I&#39;ve searched for more info about this murder, but can&#39;t find anything else. <BR>Any ideas? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12115-->
<!--Post: 12116--><!--Time: 1111603880-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12116"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 10:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mine too. I don&#39;t know that there is much outsiders can do, seeing as how KBI is working on it and have plenty of leads. I thought it interesting that they said they have lots of people to talk to, even in other states. I kinda get the impression that this will turn out to be local in nature. Someone would have to be on the ground in Beloit to find out what the &#34;streets&#34; are saying.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12116-->
<!--Post: 12119--><!--Time: 1111606539-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12119"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just sat down with a cup of coffee and went thru the mail....and I found this ad!! Wouldn&#39;t the reward bring be enough inspiration for someone to talk? Thats alot of money for a very small town, I would think SOMEBODY would be blabbing.  Maybe I should call LE there and have a visit....maybe I can learn more on the case? Something in my gut keeps telling me to pursue this... <BR> <BR>Here is the ad dated March 23, 2005 <BR><a href="http://groups.msn.com/CarolsHorseBarn/carolfleminginfo.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&amp;PhotoID=90" target=_top>http://groups.msn.com/CarolsHorseBarn/carolfleming info.msnw?action=ShowPhoto&amp;PhotoID=90</a> <BR> <BR>I hope the link works...if not let me know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12119-->
<!--Post: 12120--><!--Time: 1111607262-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12120"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 11:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lola...follow your gut dear............FOLLOW YOUR GUT....more than likely you are right..........omg wouldn&#39;t it be horrifying if the whole Rader &#40;brothers&#41; were ALL nut cases...I keep thinking of the Duck...and well...it just sounds like there is something seriously really wrong with those boys...now men. <BR>good Luck  - please keep us posted!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12120-->
<!--Post: 12121--><!--Time: 1111610351-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12121"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 12:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t ever recall seeing anything about William in Wichita? But now that I see what her business was, it may be connected to her business. I would hope you aren&#39;t right, Elsewhere. But it is a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
